### Inline Comments

**When to Comment:**
```python
# ✅ GOOD: Explaining non-obvious logic
# Use exponential backoff to avoid overwhelming the API during rate limiting
wait_time = base_delay * (2 ** retry_count)

# ✅ GOOD: Business logic reasoning
# Exclude users who signed up within last 7 days from churn calculation
# as they haven't had sufficient time to demonstrate engagement patterns
active_users = users[users['signup_date'] < (today - timedelta(days=7))]

# ✅ GOOD: Workaround explanation
# HACK: Databricks SQL warehouse sometimes returns timestamps in local timezone
# instead of UTC. Explicitly convert to UTC until bug is fixed (JIRA-123)
timestamps = pd.to_datetime(timestamps, utc=True)

# ❌ BAD: Restating what code does
# Increment counter by 1
counter += 1

# ❌ BAD: Redundant with function name
# Get user by ID
user = get_user_by_id(user_id)
```

